 q=read(R/'13_numerical_qualification/QUALIFICATION_DECISION.json');reg=rows(R/'QUALIFIED_V1_TARGET_REGISTRY.csv')[0];status=read(R/'17_reproducibility/FINAL_STATUS_CODES.json');h=read(R/'14_historical_comparison/HISTORICAL_COMPARISON.json');resource=read(R/'R8E10R2_FINAL_COUNTS.json');gate=R/'05_mechanical_preflight/PRE_SOLVE_GATE_SEALED.json'
 integrity='The complete E9 manifest, all 226 durable R1 artifacts, the R1 release seals and selected historical dependencies were rehashed successfully. The initial 729 path bindings are retained unchanged in the pre-solve audit. The expanded audit contains 908 historical bindings. The final independent verifier rechecks these files. Previous datasets, geometries, meshes, solutions and reports were preserved.\n\nThe selected recovered M1 is `06_recovered_M1/M1_C1/mesh.npz` in R1, SHA-256 `1c2656dc01850d5307402c82ccb26d2d4e24e4236cbedae729b502dd5422e8cf`. M2 is `07_refined_M2/M2_C1/mesh.npz`, SHA-256 `24190fc14d87267b4891c8eed721fac29d01d21e7e33915f1af75d604beee04b`. The original invalid M1 was excluded. R1 changed exactly one internal midside node, Gmsh tag 86669; that displacement remains present. R2 deliberately moved zero nodes and generated no CAD or meshes.'
 conversion='The Gmsh-to-SOLID187 zero-based permutation is `[0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,9,8]`. An independent implementation built the native ordering from explicit edge pairs, checking every element and all shared midside identities. Complete reversible node and element maps are supplied as CSV. Physical geometry was not adjusted to accommodate numbering.\n\nActual native counts are 145,527 nodes / 82,498 SOLID187 elements for M1 and 193,962 nodes / 109,737 SOLID187 elements for M2. Material association is 1 on both. Native CDWRITE connectivity was independently parsed and matches exactly. Each mesh has one connected volume, the expected external faces, no orphan nodes and no duplicate elements. Native database coordinates were exported through LOC arrays. Decimal parsing produces at most 1.1368683772161603e-13 mm of coordinate roundoff; this is below the 1e-12 mm serialization audit tolerance. Native coordinates are therefore not claimed to be bitwise identical. Original NPZ meshes and source arrays remain byte-identical. This numerical representation tolerance does not relax any geometry fidelity gate.'
 shape='Native fatal shape errors: zero on both meshes. M1 has two import warning messages concerning one distinct element, native 4561 / Gmsh 38861: its Jacobian determinant ratio is 35.62, above the warning limit of 30. The frozen policy rejects fatal shape errors and retains warnings separately. R1 positive sampled Jacobians and the exact positive Bernstein certificate covering the recovered support were verified by hash. No nodes or warning thresholds were changed. M2 has zero native import shape warnings.\n\nDuring solution, M1 reports two warning messages and M2 reports one. Both include an ignored redundant `SHPP,ON` command issued in `/SOLU`, where that command is unsupported. Shape checking had already been enabled in `/PREP7`, used during import and CHECK, and saved in the resumed database. The ignored duplicate command did not disable it. M1 also repeats its known shape warning. The 1,424 M2 mesher parameter-metadata warnings retained in R1 are separate from native ANSYS warnings.'
 bvp='Both meshes use the frozen standardized boundary-value problem: small-strain isotropic linear elasticity, E = 210,000 MPa, nu = 0.30, NLGEOM OFF, PCG tolerance 1e-8 and two threads. Units are mm, N and MPa. The nominal force is 100 MPa x 19 mm x 28 mm = 53,200 N per port, negative X on the left and positive X on the right. The full computational width defines this force; observation crops do not redefine it.\n\nThe common constant-X load line is Y = 30 mm, Z = -9.37643484024406 mm. The moment origin is (149.975, 30, -9.37643484024406) mm. On each actual quadratic port, the affine traction basis is b = [1, Y - 30, Z - Zline]. Solve M c = [signed F, 0, 0], where M is the area integral of b b^T. Seven-point Dunavant integration gives consistent Tri6 nodal loads. Independent 6 x 6 Gauss/Duffy integration reproduces areas, coefficients and nodal loads. Actual areas are 533.304090916 mm2 on the left and 532.301495267 mm2 on the right. Traction magnitudes remain between approximately 93.8067 and 106.0533 MPa, within the frozen 50–150 MPa envelope.\n\nThe six scalar gauges are: left rear/Ymin UX, UY, UZ; left rear/Ymax UX, UZ; left front/Ymin UX. The rigid-mode matrix has rank six. There is no full-face clamp or added lateral constraint. Each applied port passes relative force and moment limits of 1e-8. Denominators are F = 53,200 N and F t = 1,010,800 N mm.'
 equilibrium='Both native solutions completed with no fatal errors, finite displacements and stress tensors, zero constrained gauge motion and plausible positive axial deformation. Applied and recovered reaction vectors are added with their signs; moments use actual nodal coordinates and the same reference origin as the applied-load audit. The loads are self-equilibrated, so the resultant gauge reaction should be near zero rather than 53,200 N.\n\n| Quantity | M1 | M2 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Maximum displacement, mm | 0.0321961975695 | 0.0321949150388 |\n| Mean displacement magnitude, mm | 0.0136455585237 | 0.0130794068003 |\n| Relative force residual | 7.7104281e-12 | 8.1127654e-12 |\n| Moment residual / (F t) | 1.4332410e-11 | 4.5105898e-12 |\n| Native logged wall time, s | 35 | 43 |\n\nBoth equilibrium gates are 1e-5. End-node mean axial extensions are 0.02765763518 and 0.02762780666 mm. Those means sample different port node sets and are plausibility diagnostics, not an exact area-weighted compliance comparison. UX, UY, UZ ranges, signed reactions and signed moment residuals are supplied in CSV.'
 tensors='The learning target is recovered from actual solved quadratic-element displacements. For each query, locate the host Tet10, invert its quadratic surface map, form shape derivatives and the Jacobian, calculate the global displacement gradient, symmetrize it to infinitesimal strain, apply the isotropic elastic constitutive law and obtain the six physical stress components. Calculate maximum tensile principal stress as max(lambda_max, 0) before regularization. No nearest-node stress copying or averaged extrapolated nodal stress is substituted.\n\nA separate scalar-loop implementation using an explicit Voigt constitutive matrix checked 256 source points per mesh. Maximum tensor differences are 8.6203045e-11 MPa for M1 and 4.8183679e-11 MPa for M2, below the inherited 1e-7 MPa tolerance. Native ETABLE stress components were also compared with the equal-weight mean of four direct constitutive Gauss tensors on 130 M1 and 128 M2 elements. Maximum component differences are 2.9445993e-6 and 3.4867319e-6 MPa, with relative L2 approximately 1.13e-8 and 1.09e-8. This comparison recognizes the native element-average/extrapolation interpretation and is reported separately from direct surface stress. It is not used to force unlike output locations to agree.\n\nThe runtime version is established by actual ANSYS 2023 R1 logs. Explanatory field references: [ANSYS SOLID187](https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/public/Views/Secured/corp/v252/en/ans_elem/Hlp_E_SOLID187.html) and [ANSYS nodal and centroidal evaluation](https://ansyshelp.ansys.com/public/Views/Secured/corp/v242/en/ans_thry/thy_et6.html). These online documentation versions do not substitute for executed-version evidence.'
 mapping='All 68,457 original measured front points, source IDs, XYZ coordinates, 134,400 T0 triangles and frozen T0 areas were retained. Before solving, geometry-only masks fixed a 39,200-point mapping halo (992.960699490 mm2) and a 34,200-point T2 core (865.433082622 mm2). The halo excludes points within 10 mm of X ports or 2 mm of Y edges; the T2 core uses 11 mm and 3 mm respectively. Actual V1 support was verified rather than assumed from E8B.\n\nBoth meshes map all 39,200 intended halo queries, with zero failures and 100% area-weighted coverage in each region. The 29,257 exterior points remain explicitly NOT_QUERIED, with blank stress values. Full-front geometry fidelity remains supported by the separately verified R1 all-source audit. Correspondence uses actual quadratic surface inverse-XY mapping, barycentric inclusion tolerance 1e-5 and maximum distance 0.04 mm. No source coordinates are moved. M1 distance P95/max are 0.001306223 / 0.006940176 mm; M2 values are 0.000997085 / 0.005862893 mm. Maximum inverse-XY residual is 1.157e-13 mm. Host elements, barycentric coordinates, surface face IDs and actual FE projection coordinates are preserved.'
 t2='The unchanged primary T2 operator averages tensile maximum principal stress over a 1 mm three-dimensional Euclidean chord neighborhood on the same original front face, using original T0 vertex areas. The search tolerance is +1e-7 mm and valid weight coverage must be at least 1 - 1e-10. Tensile clipping precedes averaging. No projected-XY or geodesic operator is substituted.\n\nThe fixed regions are geometric proxies: normal height at least 0.5 mm above the parent plane is the weld proxy; points within 2 mm projected distance of it form the adjacent collar; remaining points form the parent proxy. They are not independently validated physical toe tracks. All 34,200 core points are valid on both meshes. Independent scalar checks used separate neighborhood queries and math.fsum for 256 points per mesh, satisfying the inherited 1e-8 MPa tolerance. Whole and regional L2 metrics and high95 IoU were also independently recomputed. L2 uses the fine M2 field in its denominator, following the inherited FE comparison convention. High95 uses an interpolated weighted CDF; the separate ML stable-step quantile convention is not used.'
 numerical='| Region | Points | Area, mm2 | M1 mean T2, MPa | M2 mean T2, MPa | Relative L2 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n'+'\n'.join(f'| {z["region"]} | {z["points"]} | {z["area_mm2"]:.6f} | {z["M1_mean_T2_MPa"]:.8f} | {z["M2_mean_T2_MPa"]:.8f} | {z["normalized_L2"]:.10f} |' for z in [q['whole']]+q['regional'])+'\n\nWhole normalized L2 is 0.003563379802 (gate 0.020); worst regional L2 is 0.006409213927 in the collar (gate 0.030); high95 area IoU is 0.982261461212 (gate 0.800). Mapping and core coverage are 1.000 (gate 0.990). High95 thresholds are 116.45477317 and 115.97620839 MPa. Maximum T2 is 148.39970694 MPa for M1 and 149.22991698 MPa for M2, giving K maxima 1.48399707 and 1.49229917 relative to 100 MPa. Raw mapped principal peaks of 245.91846 / 240.38280 MPa are reported separately and do not determine qualification.\n\nAll mandatory native, equilibrium, mapping and independent recovery checks passed. C02_V1_T2_QUALIFIED applies to a conditional two-mesh numerical target. M2 was the designated release mesh before stresses were inspected.'
 historical='Only after V1 qualified, the unchanged historical R4 C02 target was compared on the same 34,200 front source IDs. Source XYZ, IDs and triangles match exactly. Historical T0 weights differ from the V1 frozen weights only by summation roundoff: at most 1.0408341e-17 mm2, relative 4.1632471e-16. Neither file was altered. Comparison statistics use unchanged V1 weights and do not claim byte-identical historical weights. Both historical and V1 T2 operators use a 1 mm 3D chord neighborhood.\n\nHistorical mean T2 is 79.14405530 MPa versus 67.59463347 MPa for V1. The mean difference is -11.54942183 MPa; difference RMS is 12.05732712 MPa; L2 relative to historical is 0.1471313213; high95 IoU is 0.9471892167. Loadline Z changes by -0.011224694947 mm. Rear geometry, parent datum, load line, ports, closures and discretization change together. This descriptive contrast cannot be attributed solely to rear geometry or treated as physical truth. Historical targets remain separate and are not relabeled as V1.'
 limits='This is numerical verification of a standardized linear-elastic reference. E = 210 GPa, nu = 0.30 and the 100 MPa reference load are modelling assumptions; 19 mm is a documented nominal thickness, not a new measurement. Canonical X is the numerical tensile axis; independent physical calibration remains unresolved. The model represents a truncated 60 x 28 mm scan region with an assumed rear plane and synthetic caps.\n\nTwo-mesh agreement does not establish asymptotic convergence, a rigorous error bound, absence of shared bias, physical experimental validation or accurate notch metrology. Source preprocessing, raw registration, CAD fitting, the assumed rear and truncated boundary conditions can share systematic errors. Proxy regions are not validated toe tracks. No residual welding stress, plasticity, contact, thermal history, crack growth, fatigue-life prediction, grinding, new AI training or inference is included. No fresh independent generalization validation is claimed.'
 runtime=f'There were exactly three actual native preprocessing jobs and two actual SOLVE invocations, run sequentially M1 then M2. Both solutions completed; there were no repeated solves. No CAD, meshes, training runs, AI inference or external predictions were generated. Native MAPDL logged wall times are 35 and 43 seconds. The resource sampler last timestamps, approximately 33.09 and 41.39 seconds, are sampling lower bounds rather than exact workflow durations. Observed peak RSS was 1,192,153,088 / 1,477,337,088 bytes; observed private memory was 2,023,907,328 / 2,258,354,176 bytes. Sampling every two seconds can miss instantaneous peaks.\n\nMinimum observed available RAM was {resource["minimum_observed_resources"]["RAM_available_bytes"]/1024**3:.4f} GiB and commit headroom was {resource["minimum_observed_resources"]["commit_free_bytes"]/1024**3:.4f} GiB, both above the 3 GiB reserve. Disk and workspace limits were also respected. No pagefile, system-memory or licensing configuration was changed and no unrelated process was terminated.\n\nExecution incidents are preserved rather than hidden: a Python audit hook rejected the first launch before CreateProcess, so it executed no ANSYS job; the M1 completion parser initially searched for an unavailable text marker, then was corrected using the actual LOAD STEP/SUBSTEP COMPLETED and RUN COMPLETED messages. Existing native outputs were audited without solving again. The superseded host SOLVE_FAILED.json is retained as provenance and is not evidence of a failed native solution. The coordinate readback audit was corrected to disclose machine roundoff rather than falsely claim bitwise equality, without another native invocation. The expanded historical audit is separate from the unchanged pre-solve audit; the final verifier checks the original sealed bytes.'
 gate_text=f'All 17 pre-solve gates passed before either SOLVE. The gate binds 19 artifacts and records zero solves at sealing. Gate SHA-256: `{sha(gate)}`. Both mesh imports and native shape checks were complete before M1 was solved. The gate is rehashed before each solve and again by the final read-only verifier. Source support was fixed before stresses; no stress-informed mask selection occurred.'
 decision='\n'.join('- `'+v+'`' for v in status.values())+f'\n\nDesignated released target: `{reg["target_path"]}`\n\nTarget SHA-256: `{reg["target_hash"]}`\n\nTarget version: `{VERSION}`\n\nTarget semantics SHA-256: `{reg["target_semantics_hash"]}`\n\nThe next separately authorized phase may qualify G08/X10 under their own frozen geometry, mesh, BVP, resource and support gates. This does not authorize automatic production or new AI experiments.'
